<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eduard Shevardnadze</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1928">1928</a>–<a href="/years/2014">2014</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eduard Shevardnadze was First Secretary of the Communist Party of the Georgian SSR from 1972 to 1985 and Soviet foreign minister under Gorbachev from 1985 to 1990, helping to end the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>. He returned to lead independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in 1992 amid civil war and was president from 1995 until the Rose Revolution forced him out in 2003.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eduard-shevardnadze.jpg" alt="Eduard Shevardnadze" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert D. Ward · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eduard_shevardnadze_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Eduard Shevardnadze</b> headed the government from March 1992 and was president from 1995 until the Rose Revolution of 2003 removed him after fraudulent elections.</blockquote><a href="/empire/georgia">Georgia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Eduard Shevardnadze</b> led the party from 1972 to 1985.</blockquote><a href="/state/georgian-ssr">Georgian SSR</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Mamati, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42.02,42.03&amp;year=1983" aria-label="Mamati on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5571 668 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Eduard Shevardnadze"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6021 938h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6021 938h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42.02,42.03&amp;year=1983">What was here in 1983? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
